---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Which Has More — Max Vogt">
  <main id="top" class="page-container">
    <header class="section-pad fade-up">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-6">
        <label class="toggle text-base">
          <a class="text-[1.25rem] font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] hover:text-[var(--color-primary)]" href="/">Max.</a>
          <input type="checkbox" aria-label="Toggle dark mode" data-theme-toggle />
          <span class="toggle-icons" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="toggle-icon icon-moon">◑</span>
          </span>
        </label>
        <nav class="flex items-center gap-8 text-base">
          <a class="nav-link transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-[var(--color-primary)]" href="/">Work</a>
          <a class="nav-link transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-[var(--color-primary)]" href="/about">About</a>
          <a
            class="nav-link transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-[var(--color-primary)]"
            href="https://www.instagram.com/maaxvogt/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
          >
            Fun
          </a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="section-pad fade-up delay-1">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
        <h1 class="text-[clamp(2.8rem,6vw,4.6rem)]">Which Has More</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-muted max-w-[52rem]">
          A minimal interactive game centered around comparison logic and decision-making, designed
          to provide immediate feedback through clear interaction and intentional simplicity. The
          project explores how small design choices influence understanding, engagement, and user confidence.
        </p>
        <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3 text-sm">
          <div>
            <p class="text-muted uppercase tracking-[0.2em]">Role</p>
            <p>Designer & Developer</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-muted uppercase tracking-[0.2em]">Team</p>
            <p>Solo project</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-muted uppercase tracking-[0.2em]">Duration</p>
            <p>~1–2 weeks (concept, design, implementation)</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad fade-up delay-2">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Intent</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted">
            Which Has More was created as a design exercise, not as a feature-rich game.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            The goal was to explore how users reason about comparisons when provided with limited
            information and immediate feedback, and how clarity in interaction design can guide
            decision-making without explicit instructions.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            The project intentionally avoids complexity in favor of focus, responsiveness, and learnability.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Design & Interaction Approach</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted">
            The game is built around a small set of deliberate design constraints:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-muted space-y-2">
            <li>Single, clear interaction loop</li>
            <li>Immediate feedback</li>
            <li>Minimal visual language</li>
            <li>Low cognitive load</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-muted">
            These choices emphasize intuition over instruction.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Learning and Growth</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted">
            This project sharpened my sensitivity to user experience at a micro-interaction level:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-muted space-y-2">
            <li>Designing interfaces where clarity emerges through use, not documentation</li>
            <li>Balancing simplicity with engagement</li>
            <li>Understanding how feedback timing influences user confidence</li>
            <li>Treating UX decisions as first-class engineering decisions</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-muted">
            It reinforced that even small projects can surface important lessons about usability and design intent.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Takeaway</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted font-semibold">
            Good interaction design is not about adding features — it is about removing friction.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            Which Has More demonstrates how intentional constraints, clear feedback, and simplicity can
            create experiences that feel intuitive, satisfying, and self-explanatory.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-16 text-right">
        <a href="#top" class="nav-link text-base">Back to Top ↑</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
        <h2>Let's get in touch</h2>
        <p class="text-muted">
          HMU for work, coffee, or if you just want to talk.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-6 text-sm">
          <a
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-transparent transition-colors duration-200 hover:border-[var(--color-primary)]"
            href="https://github.com/maaxvogt/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
          >
            GitHub
          </a>
          <a
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-transparent transition-colors duration-200 hover:border-[var(--color-primary)]"
            href="mailto:mavoxgt@gmail.com"
          >
            Mail
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted">Designed and coded by Max Vogt</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
